Here's the Lego logic explained:

**Phase 1 — Web Asistan (20 components, ~8 weeks, generates revenue)**

This builds the FOUNDATION that everything else sits on. You get: Kubernetes + ArgoCD + monitoring (Grafana/Prometheus) as infrastructure. MariaDB + Qdrant + Redis + MinIO as storage. Keycloak for multi-tenant auth. Kong + FastAPI + WebSockets as the API layer. LiteLLM + Ollama as the AI core. LlamaIndex + a basic Product Agent for catalog search. The embeddable widget, self-service dashboard, landing page, and iyzico/Stripe billing. File uploads as the only data source.

This is a complete, working, revenue-generating SaaS product. A ceramic manufacturer uploads their product catalog, gets a chatbot on their website, pays ₺5,000/month.

**Phase 2 — CWF (19 components added, builds on Phase 1)**

Everything from Phase 1 stays. Now you add the manufacturing intelligence layer: LangGraph + LangChain + n8n for complex agent orchestration. vLLM for self-hosted GPU inference. MLflow, Prompt Store, Cross Check for AI operations. The MCP layer (MariaDB, Qdrant, ClickHouse MCP servers) so agents query data through a standard protocol. MariaDB Galera clustering for HA. ClickHouse for analytics. Apache NiFi + Airbyte + Spark for enterprise data ingestion. CWF microservices + Schema Registry. Full Next.js app + Superset + OpenWebUI. Loki + OpenTelemetry + Wireguard for production ops. OPA + Hallucination Guard + Vault for security. ARMES and IoT-Ignite as optional data sources.

This is a full Chat With Factory deployment — everything Kale Group uses, deployable for any manufacturer.

**Phase 3 — Astra EAIP (16 components added, builds on Phase 2)**

Everything from Phase 1 and 2 stays. Now you add enterprise capabilities: RLS Core Engine + Guardrails AI + Presidio + Entra ID federation for enterprise security. Temporal for durable long-running processes. UC-specific agents and services (Financial BI, Inventory Intelligence, Board Governance, Multi-Channel Product). The full data quality layer (Soda Core, dbt Core, OpenMetadata, LLM Enrichment). Redpanda + Debezium for CDC streaming. Medallion architecture (Bronze/Silver/Gold). Langfuse + Evidently AI for LLM observability and model drift. Azure OpenAI as optional fallback. SAP, SharePoint, Salesforce, PIM, SQL Server MCP servers. B2B Portal, Usta Portal, Teams Bot channels.

This is the full Astra Holding enterprise platform — 4 use cases, 9 external sources, RLS, staged delivery.

**The key architectural decisions in the convergence:**

| **Decision** | **What won** | **Why** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary DB | MariaDB Galera | Your team's DNA, ARMES compatible, Galera clustering |
| Auth | Keycloak | Fully OSS, no Microsoft dependency. Entra ID added as federation in P3 |
| Orchestrator | NiFi | Team expertise. File Upload pipeline in P1, full NiFi in P2 |
| API Gateway | Kong | Both CWF and Astra already use it |
| BI/Viz | Superset | CWF already uses it, more capable than Metabase |
| LLM Proxy | LiteLLM | Not in CWF but essential for multi-model routing |
| Caching | Redis | From CWF, missing in original Astra design |
| Secrets | HashiCorp Vault | From CWF, production-grade |
| CD | ArgoCD | From CWF, GitOps standard |
| Monitoring | Grafana + Prometheus + Loki + OpenTelemetry | CWF's stack is more complete |
| Agent safety | Hallucination Guard (P2) + Guardrails AI (P3) | Both, at different levels |
| Prompt mgmt | Prompt Store | From CWF, critical for quality over time |
| Output verify | Cross Check | From CWF, validates LLM against known data |
| MCP | Dedicated layer | From CWF, cleaner than direct DB calls |

**Total: 55 components across 10 layers. 20 in Phase 1, 19 added in Phase 2, 16 added in Phase 3. Nothing gets thrown away. Every phase builds on the previous one like Lego.**

