Updated. The Phase 1 Web Asistan section now has 5 frontend tasks instead of 2, all assigned to P5 (Full-Stack Dev) in Month 1:

- **Embeddable widget** (5 pd) — the JS snippet, chat UI, product card rendering

- **Self-service onboarding + upload wizard** (4 pd) — first-time signup, catalog upload flow

- **Admin panel** (5 pd) — content management (upload new catalogs, replace old, see what's indexed, delete, re-index), widget configuration (colors, branding, welcome message, CTA buttons), embed code manager with domain list and preview

- **Training/correction UI** (4 pd) — thumbs up/down on every response, Q&A override panel for manual answers ("Kargo süresi ne kadar?" type questions), feedback loop that improves the chatbot

- **Analytics dashboard** (3 pd) — conversations/day, top products asked about, unanswered questions, contact form submissions, ROI tracking

- **Widget embed manager** (2 pd) — copy embed code, see deployed domains, live preview

P10 (the new hire) takes over from Month 2 with "Admin panel v2" as their first task — polishing what P5 built in the sprint and iterating based on early customer feedback.

Phase 1 effort is now 111 person-days (was 100), with Phase 3 adjusted to keep the overall total at ~1,085 pd.